  "result": "All 5 tests pass across both test files.\n\nChanges to `netgraph/graph.py`:\n\n- **remove_edge** discards the edge from both adjacency sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns whether the edge existed. Self-loops are handled by the same code since both discards hit the same set.\n- **degree** returns the size of the node's adjacency set, so a self-loop counts once.\n- **connected_components** does an iterative depth-first search from each unvisited node in ascending order. Visiting starts in ascending order means components come out ordered by smallest node, and each component is sorted before being appended.\n\nAll three methods bounds-check their node arguments and raise `IndexError` like the existing API.",
